      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, a typical starting dose. It's also the usual choice for frail or elderly patients, or those with hepatic impairment.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written**, if the dose is intentional. If so, please confirm it and give a brief rationale. I'll add that to the order note.\n\nIf 10 mg isn't controlling the blood pressure, adding a second agent is usually preferred to going above 10 mg. Good options include an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-like diuretic.\n\nTell me which option you'd like and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
